<section id="Pt0.A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.B </span>Appendix Derivations of Computational Cost</h2>

<div id="Pt0.A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The task to be completed by a generative transformer is as follows: Let <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> be a vocabulary consisting of <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math> unique tokens, <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\{x_{1},x_{2},...,x_{n}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\{x_{1},x_{2},...,x_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with one of the tokens <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> being the stop token.
Let <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}=(y_{1},y_{2},...,y_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}=(y_{1},y_{2},...,y_{L})</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary sequence of tokens from <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and the number of elements in <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=|\mathbf{y}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=|\mathbf{y}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> be a probability distribution over all tokens in <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> parametrised by <math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
The task of the transformer is to model the joint probability of a token sequence:
<math id="Pt0.A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}(\mathbf{y})=\Pi_{i=1}^{L}p_{\theta}(y_{i}|y_{1},y_{2},...,y_{i-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\mathbf{y})=\Pi_{i=1}^{L}p_{\theta}(y_{i}|y_{1},y_{2},...,y_{i-1})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<section id="Pt0.A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.B.1 </span>Transformer Architecture</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The transformer architecture was originally published in 2017 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> which contained both encoder and decoder stacks. However most Large Language Models are pre-layer-normalisation, decoder-only Transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>.
The decoder-only transformer consists of several components. The first is an embedding matrix<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            The embedding matrix must have dimension <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{vocab}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{vocab}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></span> which converts input tokens to vector embeddings.
Then a positional encoder adds either fixed sinusoidal or learned values, to each vector embedding to indicate its position in the sequence.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The multi-head attention block then begins with layer normalisation before a multi-head attention.
The block contains matrices <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> indicates corresponding to the hth attention head.
The (positionally encoded) token embeddings from the previous layer matrices are multiplied by these matrices to create the query, key and value matrices, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            Each of the <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> matrices must have dimension <math id="footnote2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math>. As there are <math id="footnote2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{heads}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{heads}}</annotation></semantics></math> of each this can be concatenated into one <math id="footnote2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="footnote2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> for more efficient computation. Usually <math id="footnote2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}=n_{\text{heads}}d_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}=n_{\text{heads}}d_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math> in which case <math id="footnote2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="footnote2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="footnote2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> have size <math id="footnote2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>.
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{h}K_{h}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>h</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{h}K_{h}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated to create a matrix which contains scores indicating how much each token should attend to every other token <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>.
In the decoder only architecture, a mask is applied to the top-right triangle of this matrix, converting the values to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty</annotation></semantics></math> to prevent tokens to attending to future tokens <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>.
Softmax is then applied before multiplying by the value matrix <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> to create <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> output matrices <math id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>.
These output matrices are concatenated and passed through a linear layer to create the final output from the attention layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">At this stage most decoder-only transformers have a post residual connection layer which adds the embedding that was passed into the attention block to the output of the attention layer before the next block’s pre-layer normalisation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>.
The same process is used to add the input of a feed forward network block to its output <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>.
The feed forward network increase the dimension of the embedding, apply non-linear activation functions to each entry, before contracting back to the model dimension <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>.
Then there is a final residual connection layer.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These multi-head attention and feed forward blocks combine to form a layer.
Typical LLMs have between 6 and 200 layers depending on their size.
After all of the layers there is a final normalisation layer and then a linear layer uses a weight matrix to project the output into the vocabulary space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>. A common parameter efficient implementation called tied input-output embeddings uses the transpose of the embedding matrix to obtain the final embedding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>.
This gives each token a score for each entry in the vocabulary, which a final softmax function converts to a probability distribution for the next token <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.B.2 </span>Theoretical FLOPs Calculations</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper we calculate the theoretical FLOPs required for the open source models used, DeepSeek R1, Llama-3 405B, Phi-4, Gemma-3 12B and Falcon-3 10B. Note that these models with the exception of Phi-4 do not use biases in their linear layers.
As this only contributes a small number of parameters to the model and FLOPs at inference we will ignore these for all models.
These models all use RoPE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> for positional embedding and RMSNorm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">64</a>]</cite> for normalisation.
DeepSeek uses Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, however we ignore this technique in our calculations as its primary impact is reducing the memory usage of the KV cache. We acknowledge that for long sequences MLA could reduce the FLOPs and that our calculation does not capture this effect.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Kaplan provides a method for approximating the number of floating point operations (FLOPs) required for a forward pass of a decoder only transformer using the following notation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>:
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">d</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#005A9C">model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the embedding size, also known as the dimension of the residual stream,
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">d</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#005A9C">ff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the expanded dimension of the feed forward layer,
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">d</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#005A9C">attn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the dimension of each attention head, given by <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}=n_{\text{heads}}d_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}=n_{\text{heads}}d_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{heads}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">n</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#005A9C">heads</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{heads}}</annotation></semantics></math> is number of attention heads in each multi-head attention block,
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">n</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#005A9C">ctx</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}</annotation></semantics></math> number of tokens in the input context,
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">n</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#005A9C">max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the maximum context length,
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{layer}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">n</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#005A9C">layer</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{layer}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of layers,
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is the Group Query Attention ratio and
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">n</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#005A9C">vocab</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of tokens in the vocabulary, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, therefore <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{vocab}}=|V|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{vocab}}=|V|</annotation></semantics></math>. We will use
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the total number of parameters in the model (model size), which, assuming tied input-output embeddings, RoPE positional embeddings and RMSNorm Normalisation is given by
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\approx d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+n_{\text{layers}}(2d_{\text{model}}+(1+2/g)n_{\text{heads}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{attn}}+n_{\text{heads}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{attn}}+3d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}})+d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layers</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\approx d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+n_{\text{layers}}(2d_{\text{model}}+(1+2/g)n_{\text{heads}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{attn}}+n_{\text{heads}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{attn}}+3d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}})+d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
simplifying gives
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\approx d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+n_{\text{layers}}d_{\text{model}}(2+(2+2/g)d_{\text{model}}+3d_{\text{ff}})+d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layers</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\approx d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+n_{\text{layers}}d_{\text{model}}(2+(2+2/g)d_{\text{model}}+3d_{\text{ff}})+d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
            Note that <math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{max}}d_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{max}}d_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math> values must be precomputed for RoPE but these are not learned parameters and do not count towards the parameter count</span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We will make the same assumption that the computational cost of multiplying two matrices of dimensions <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\times b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\times b</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\times c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\times c</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2abc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2abc</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>. This is because for each of the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\times c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\times c</annotation></semantics></math> entries in the output matrix we perform <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> multiplications and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b-1\approx b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b-1\approx b</annotation></semantics></math> additions. However due to causal masking in attention, the upper diagonal of a square matrix (assuming <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=c</annotation></semantics></math>) does not always need to be calculated, in this case the number of FLOPs required for calculation is <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ba(a+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ba(a+1)</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We start by considering the computational cost of the first token output. The total computational cost of processing the entire input sequence to generate the first output token will be given by the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=C_{1_{\text{embedding}}}+n_{\text{layer}}(C_{1_{\text{attn}}}+C_{1_{\text{ff}}})+C_{1_{\text{ouput}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>embedding</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>ouput</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=C_{1_{\text{embedding}}}+n_{\text{layer}}(C_{1_{\text{attn}}}+C_{1_{\text{ff}}})+C_{1_{\text{ouput}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The first step is to convert the context tokens to vector embeddings. As these are one hot encoded this requires only lookup operations and therefore technically do not contribute any FLOPs to the overall computational cost.
Traditionally position embeddings were added to each of the input token embeddings uses <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1_{\text{embedding}}}=n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>embedding</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1_{\text{embedding}}}=n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs (addition operations) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>, before the first attention block.
This is a very small contribution to the overall computational cost, so some authors ignore this <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>.
The models in this study use RoPE which actually applies positional embeddings within the attention blocks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite>.
Therefore the cost of embedding will be calculated in these sections and there is no cost (in FLOPs) to calculate the initial embeddings, so <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1_{\text{embedding}}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>embedding</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1_{\text{embedding}}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">After the tokens are converted to vector embeddings the first Layer normalisation block is applied. For each embedding vector the RMSNorm calculates the square of each entry (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> multiplications), sums all the entries (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}-1</annotation></semantics></math> additions), divides the sum by the number of entries (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> division), takes the square root and inverts the result (approximately <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs), scales each entry by this factor (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> divisions) and multiplies the result by a learned scaling parameters <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> multiplications). This has a total cost of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d_{\text{model}}+2\approx 4d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d_{\text{model}}+2\approx 4d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> per input token <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>.
Given a context length of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}</annotation></semantics></math>, this results in <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">In the attention block first the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> matrices must be computed by multiplying the vector embeddings (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>) by the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{V}</annotation></semantics></math> matrices (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>) which requires <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Note that models which use Group Query Attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> reduce this cost by reusing (sharing) Key and Value matrices for a <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> Query matrices.
In this case the cost is reduced to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2+4/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2+4/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Then RoPE is applied to the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}</annotation></semantics></math> rows of the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> matrices corresponding to each token.
A rotation matrix is applied to each pair of elements in the rows in the Q and K matrices. This makes a total of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n_{\text{heads}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n_{\text{heads}}</annotation></semantics></math> vectors to which it is applied.
The cost of applying the rotation is <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3d_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3d_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math>FLOPs per entry, two multiplications and one addition per attention dimension.
Therefore the total cost of RoPE for one head is <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{attn}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs. Taking into account Query Group Attention and summing over all of the heads gives <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3+3/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3+3/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>FLOPs.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Computing the elements of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> not covered by the causal mask requires <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs
<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
              
              
              
            Notice that the true derivation calculates attention for each of <math id="footnote4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{heads}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{heads}}</annotation></semantics></math> heads of dimension <math id="footnote4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{attn}}=d_{\text{model}}/n_{\text{heads}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{attn}}=d_{\text{model}}/n_{\text{heads}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="footnote4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{attn}})=n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{attn}})=n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> which reduces to the same result as the simplified concatenated model.</span></span></span>
and scaling (element wise division) requires one FLOP per element: <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5\times n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5\times n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
When considering the FLOPs used by softmax function we must consider each of the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{heads}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{heads}}</annotation></semantics></math> attention head separately.
For each head the softmax is applied to each row of the matrix so all <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> entries not covered by the mask.
This leads to a total cost of approximately 10 FLOPs per entry, depending on how Softmax is implemented.
Therefore the total cost of this across all heads is <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Multiplying the result (a <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}\times n_{\text{ctx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}\times n_{\text{ctx}}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix) by the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>) matrix then uses <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs as the above diagonal entries of the former matrix are 0.
Then this output is multiplied by a weight matrix (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>) at a cost of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Adding the original vector embedding to this output requires <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Therefore each attention block (including layer normalization) requires <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1_{\text{attn}}}=(4+4/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}+(8+3/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}+2n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}+5.5n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1_{\text{attn}}}=(4+4/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}+(8+3/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}+2n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}+5.5n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The feed forward layer begins with a Layer normalisation (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs).
The the models that we use in this paper use either SwiGLU or GeGLU activation functions.
To take into account both of these we introduce a new parameter <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{$n_{A}$}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">n</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C">n</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#005A9C;" mathcolor="#005A9C" mathsize="0.980em">A</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{$n_{A}$}}</annotation></semantics></math> which is the number of FLOPs per application of the activation function.
<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{A}\approx 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{A}\approx 6</annotation></semantics></math> for SwiGLU (SiLU) and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{A}\approx 10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{A}\approx 10</annotation></semantics></math> for GeGLU (GeLU) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">46</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>.
In either case the input matrix (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>) is multiplied by both a gate matrix <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{gate}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{gate}}</annotation></semantics></math> and an up-projection matrix <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Both of these matrices have size (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}\times d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math>) and both matrix multiplications combined cost <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Then the SiLU/GeLU activation functions must then be applied to each of the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> entries of the matrix resulting from multiplying the normalised input by <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{gate}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{gate}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the cost for this is <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{A}n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{A}n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Then element wise multiplication between the result and the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix costs <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Finally multiplication by the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{down}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{down}}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix requires another <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Adding the feed-forward input vector embedding to this output requires <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs, resulting in a total of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1_{\text{ff}}}=5n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}+6n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1_{\text{ff}}}=5n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}+6n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for the feed forward block.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">To convert the vector embedding into an output over the vocabulary there are three steps.
First, there is a final RMSNorm layer, however this time only the embedding corresponding to the final token needs to be calculated so the cost is <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
The second step is to multiply this final token embedding (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>) by the transpose of the embedding matrix (<math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}\times n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}\times n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math>) which costs <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
The third step is to apply the softmax function to the final row<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
              
              
              
            Note that at inference time the proceeding token probability distribution only needs to be computed for the final input token.
At training time this softmax would have to be applied to all <math id="footnote5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{ctx}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{ctx}}</annotation></semantics></math> tokens.</span></span></span>,
which has an approximate cost of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs. Therefore <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1_{\text{output}}}=4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>output</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1_{\text{output}}}=4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore the approximate cost for the first token is:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1_{\text{embedding}}}+n_{\text{layer}}(C_{1_{\text{attn}}}+C_{1_{\text{ff}}})+C_{1_{\text{output}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>embedding</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mn>1</mn><mtext>output</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1_{\text{embedding}}}+n_{\text{layer}}(C_{1_{\text{attn}}}+C_{1_{\text{ff}}})+C_{1_{\text{output}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0+n_{\text{layer}}[(4+4/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}+(8+3/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}+2n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}+5.5n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)]+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0+n_{\text{layer}}[(4+4/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}^{2}+(8+3/g)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}+2n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)d_{\text{model}}+5.5n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)]+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n_{\text{layer}}(5n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}+6n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{ff}})+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n_{\text{layer}}(5n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}+6n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)n_{\text{ctx}}d_{\text{ff}})+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle n_{\text{ctx}}n_{\text{layer}}[d_{\text{model}}([4+4/g]d_{\text{model}}+18+2n_{\text{ctx}}+6d_{\text{ff}})+5.5n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}})]+4d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5.5</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n_{\text{ctx}}n_{\text{layer}}[d_{\text{model}}([4+4/g]d_{\text{model}}+18+2n_{\text{ctx}}+6d_{\text{ff}})+5.5n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+1)+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}})]+4d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+n_{\text{vocab}}(2d_{\text{model}}+10)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+n_{\text{vocab}}(2d_{\text{model}}+10)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p">As long as sufficient memory is available, the cost for each subsequent token can be reduced using KV caching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. We will say the total computational cost for each token after the first is given by <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}=C_{i_{\text{embedding}}}+n_{\text{layer}}(C_{i_{\text{attn}}}+C_{i_{\text{ff}}})+C_{i_{\text{output}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>embedding</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}=C_{i_{\text{embedding}}}+n_{\text{layer}}(C_{i_{\text{attn}}}+C_{i_{\text{ff}}})+C_{i_{\text{output}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to before <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i_{\text{embedding}}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>embedding</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i_{\text{embedding}}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">The layer normalisation cost for this one token is <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Due to KV caching, only one row needs to be calculated for each Query, Key and Value matrix requiring <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2+4/g)d_{\text{model}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2+4/g)d_{\text{model}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Applying RoPE to the new Q and K rows costs <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3+3/g)d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3+3/g)d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Only one new attention row needs to be calculated by taking an inner product of the new Query vector with each of the cached <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> vectors plus the new <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> vector. Therefore the new attention row requires <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)d_{\text{attn}}=2d_{\text{model}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)d_{\text{attn}}=2d_{\text{model}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Scaling and applying the softmax costs an additional <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Multiplying by the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> matrix costs <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)d_{\text{attn}}=2d_{\text{model}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)d_{\text{attn}}=2d_{\text{model}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
After concatenation the resulting vector will be multiplied by <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{O}</annotation></semantics></math> which costs another <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d_{\text{model}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d_{\text{model}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs.
Finally adding the residual has a cost of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs. Therefore <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i_{attn}}=(8+3g)d_{\text{model}}+8d_{\text{model}}^{2}+4(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)d_{\text{model}}+11n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i_{attn}}=(8+3g)d_{\text{model}}+8d_{\text{model}}^{2}+4(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)d_{\text{model}}+11n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">The feed forward layer only needs to act on the ith token, reducing the cost of layer normalisation to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{gate}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>gate</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{gate}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>up</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{up}}</annotation></semantics></math> multiplications to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs each, the application of activation functions to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{A}d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{A}d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs, element wise multiplication to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math>, multiplication by the <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{down}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>down</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{down}}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the addition of the residual embedding to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> FLOPs respectively. Therefore <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i_{\text{ff}}}=5d_{\text{model}}+6d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i_{\text{ff}}}=5d_{\text{model}}+6d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The computational cost of the output layer is unchanged, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i_{\text{output}}}=4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i_{\text{output}}}=4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore the approximate cost for the ith token is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{i}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{i}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{i_{\text{embedding}}}+n_{\text{layer}}(C_{i_{\text{attn}}}+C_{i_{\text{ff}}})+C_{i_{\text{output}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>embedding</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>attn</mtext></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{i_{\text{embedding}}}+n_{\text{layer}}(C_{i_{\text{attn}}}+C_{i_{\text{ff}}})+C_{i_{\text{output}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{i}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{i}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0+n_{\text{layer}}[(8+3g)d_{\text{model}}+(4+4/g)d_{\text{model}}^{2}+4d_{\text{model}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)+11n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)]+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0+n_{\text{layer}}[(8+3g)d_{\text{model}}+(4+4/g)d_{\text{model}}^{2}+4d_{\text{model}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)+11n_{\text{heads}}(n_{\text{ctx}}+i)]+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n_{\text{layer}}[5d_{\text{model}}+6d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}}]+4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n_{\text{layer}}[5d_{\text{model}}+6d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}}]+4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{i}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{i}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle n_{\text{layer}}[(13+3/g)d_{\text{model}}+(4+4/g)d_{\text{model}}^{2}+4d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{ctx}}+11n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}+6d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}}]+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle n_{\text{layer}}[(13+3/g)d_{\text{model}}+(4+4/g)d_{\text{model}}^{2}+4d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{ctx}}+11n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}+6d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}}]+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle i(4d_{\text{model}}+11n_{\text{heads}})n_{\text{layer}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle i(4d_{\text{model}}+11n_{\text{heads}})n_{\text{layer}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">For future calculations we will divide <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> into two components, one that is independent of <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> called <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a second which is proportional to <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="iC_{ic}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">iC_{ic}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}=C_{i0}+iC_{ic}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}=C_{i0}+iC_{ic}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{ic}=(4d_{\text{model}}+11n_{\text{heads}})n_{\text{layer}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{ic}=(4d_{\text{model}}+11n_{\text{heads}})n_{\text{layer}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i0}=n_{\text{layer}}[(13+3/g)d_{\text{model}}+(4+4/g)d_{\text{model}}^{2}+4d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{ctx}}+11n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}+6d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}}]+4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>layer</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>heads</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>ctx</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>ff</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>vocab</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i0}=n_{\text{layer}}[(13+3/g)d_{\text{model}}+(4+4/g)d_{\text{model}}^{2}+4d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{ctx}}+11n_{\text{heads}}n_{\text{ctx}}+6d_{\text{model}}d_{\text{ff}}+(n_{A}+1)d_{\text{ff}}]+4d_{\text{model}}+2d_{\text{model}}n_{\text{vocab}}+10n_{\text{vocab}}</annotation></semantics></math>
If the number of output tokens is length <math id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p15.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{out}}</annotation></semantics></math> then the total cost of inference is given by</p>
<table id="Pt0.A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\text{total}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\text{total}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}+\sum_{i=2}^{n_{\text{out}}}C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}+\sum_{i=2}^{n_{\text{out}}}C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\text{total}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\text{total}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{1}+(n_{\text{out}}-1)C_{i0}+\frac{(n_{\text{out}}+2)(n_{\text{out}}-1)}{2}C_{ic}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>out</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{1}+(n_{\text{out}}-1)C_{i0}+\frac{(n_{\text{out}}+2)(n_{\text{out}}-1)}{2}C_{ic}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p">Note that DeepSeek is a mixture of Experts Model. This does not impact the attention layers, but means that there are many sets of expert Feed Forward Network layers, eight of which are used to respond to any given query.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.C </span>Appendix - Contamination Check</h2>

<div id="Pt0.A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the start of the experiment contamination was not a significant risk. The ProntoQA dataset had only just been released and it was not widely used. Now the benchmark is well cited. Also as informal preliminary contamination test, the authors asked frontier models about ProntoQA in 2025, they knew about it and can describe it.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In order to check for contamination we replaced all of the concept names, property families and proper nouns in the default ProntoQA script with ones that do not appear. For example ‘animal’ was replaced with ‘angel’. Then the highest performing Frontier Model and the small LLMs experiments were run again on the newly generated ‘original’ examples.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A3.T3" class="ltx_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure ltx_flex_table">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="Pt0.A3.T3.3" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span id="Pt0.A3.T3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Frontier LLM</span></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
